id: SCA-026
title: Git submodule from suspicious host
category: supply-chain
severity: warning
engine: pattern
target:
  filenames: .gitmodules
  exclude_paths: .git/
patterns:
  - regex: url\s*=\s*http://
    message: Submodule uses insecure HTTP — vulnerable to MITM attacks. CVE-2024-32002 demonstrated how crafted submodules can achieve RCE during clone.
  - regex: url\s*=\s*https?://[^/]
    message: Verify submodule host is trusted. Submodules from unknown hosts may serve malicious code. Pin submodules to specific commits.
fix: Only use submodules from trusted hosts (github.com, gitlab.com, bitbucket.org). Pin submodules to specific commits. Use HTTPS only.
